Successful Azure environments continuously evolve based on operational experience.

A continuous feedback loop generally follows these stages:

* Monitor
* Measure
* Analyze
* Improve
* Validate
* Repeat

Feedback sources include:

* Monitoring alerts
* Incident reports
* User feedback
* Cost reports
* Security findings
* Performance metrics

# Real-Life Example:
For example, repeated storage latency alerts may result in storage optimization or architecture improvements.

# Real-Life Use Case:
A real-life use case is cloud operations teams using monthly review meetings to prioritize infrastructure improvements.

Continuous feedback drives operational excellence.
